  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership CDEL fund with the Asian Development Bank and the Rockefeller foundation which will be used to help cities plan for and invest in to reduce the impacts of weather related changes and extreme events</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Partnership CDEL fund with the Asian Development Bank and the Rockefeller foundation which will be used to help cities plan for and invest in to reduce the impacts of weather related changes and extreme events is a component of Managing Climate Risks for Urban Poor reported by FCDO with a funding type of 109 - Multilateral organisation and a budget of &#xa3;41,500,000. This project benefits Asia, regional. It works in the following sector(s): Environmental policy and administrative management, Urban development and management.</narrative>
  </description>
